# C3DC Explore — object repository (`ObjectRepository/C3DC/`)

Use when adding or fixing **Explore filter locators** and **`select_filter()`** calls in C3DC tests. For **Memgraph tab Cypher** in xlsx workbooks, see **`c3dc-memgraph-cypher.mdc`**.

Loaded by `Commons/object_repository.py`. Keys match Katalon paths minus app name.

## Files

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `filters/study.yaml` | Study facet |
| `filters/diagnosis.yaml` | Diagnosis |
| `filters/demographics.yaml` | Race, sex at birth |
| `filters/survival.yaml` | First event, survival status, cause of death |
| `filters/treatment.yaml` | Treatment type, agent |
| `filters/treatment_resp.yaml` | Response, category, system |
| `filters/samples.yaml` | Anatomic site, tumor spatial extent |
| `statbar.yaml`, `result_tabs.yaml`, `navbar.yaml` | Explore chrome |
| `static/*.yaml` | Home / About / Data model |

## Filter YAML shape

```yaml
page: Filters/Demographics
groups:
  Demographics/Race:
    facet: (//*[text()="Demographics"])[1]
    dropdown: //*[@id='Race' and @role='button']
    checkboxes:
      MidEastOrNorthAfrican: //*[@id="checkbox_Race_Middle Eastern or North African"]
```

- **`groups` key** = first argument to `select_filter()` (e.g. `Study/dbGaP_Accession`, `Treatment/TreatmentType`, `Samples/TumorSpatialExtent` for UI **Tumor Spatial Extent**).
- **`checkboxes` key** = second argument to `select_filter()` (short PascalCase token, **not** the full UI label).
- **Checkbox id pattern:** `checkbox_<Facet label>_<value>` (spaces as in UI, e.g. `checkbox_Treatment Type_Radiation`, `checkbox_Tumor Spatial Extent_Metastatic`).
- **`dropdown`:** `@id` must match Explore facet sub-panel (verify in browser if UI renames, e.g. Tumor Spatial Extent vs legacy “Tumor classification”). Many facets use `@role='button'` on the dropdown control.
- **Samples filters:** each group uses `facet: (//*[text()="Samples"])[2]` — **`[1]` is usually the result tab**; `[2]` is the left filter category (same pattern as `Study` / `Survival` with inline `facet`).
- **`other`:** scroll helpers for long lists (see `study.yaml` dbGaP scroll).

If `select_filter` fails with unknown checkbox, add the value under the right `groups` entry — do not hardcode XPath in tests.

